From dea321f4ab40a17dfb8a007af31748749868c5c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:09:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] WIP HC16: make the HC normalized stream xn BF16-only

The xn producer (fused rms_norm+mul) now skips its F32 store when every
consumer reads the BF16 copy: the down GEMM (already bf16), dsv4_hc_pre
src[0] (new xbf16 arm) and the tiny-M F32 inject GEMMs (new bf16 X read).

xn is the one activation with delayed consumers, so its copy gets a
dedicated producer slot (4): the generic slot 0 is reused by every other
activation copy in between, and dsv4_hc_pre writes its own output there.

PPL c2048 10.5771 (HC16=0) / 10.6015 (HC16=1), greedy re-baselined.
---
